                        "username": "Pavithrab7"
                    },
                    "message": "What happens when `cc != PLDM_SUCCESS`? The earlier code used to print an error trace. Shouldn't we keep the same and print the completion code value?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_base_cmd.cpp",
                    "line": 155,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Rajeev Ranjan",
                        "email": "ranjan.rajeev1609@gmail.com",
                        "username": "rajeeranjan"
                    },
                    "message": "the method below is translating the cc into human readable completion code - \n```\nfillCompletionCode(cc, data, PLDM_BASE)\n```\nAnd the same would be printed in the response, so there's no change in the behaviour.\n\nAlso we can use verbose flag to get the raw Tx/Rx"
                }
